sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Danio albolineatus Schnakenberg wavelength at 37 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 85.5/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2, superseding the Pass 1 audit. Same Schnakenberg system. Fastest pearl-danio mode 3.6858e-05 m. Danio aesculapii bars at 4.180e-05 m (orientation ratio 4.56, std 0.327). Danio margaritatus spots at 3.422e-05 m (std 0.707). Equal-diffusion control σ_max = −0.137 and the field decays (std 6e-6). Dispersion goodness-of-fit Pearson r = 0.9999999999999999, RMSE 6.9e-16. All-band radial spectrum versus linear theory r = 0.9799. Restricting to bins with σ(k) > 0 lowers that correlation to 0.936 (R1): the unstable band is narrow and the weakly grown mode is still near the noise floor. FFT wavelengths at seeds 3161, 7 and 99 are 35759, 34513 and 36860 nm (CV 0.027) (R2). Specimen depth/length 0.221 versus FishBase 0.250; tight ROI 0.226; circularity 0.321. GIF computer-vision similarity to the Commons photograph is 96.0 (12 frames, 680 px). A full-frame cellular-field ablation scores 85.2. Weighted overall 85.5/100. R3–R5 remain open. Overall 85.5/100 (faithfulness 85.0, reproducibility 86.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/danio_albolineatus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 433658 B, 1584×1224 px, artifact_sha256 056fbfdf9ee2dc34c7d28dd6b66a73ebcc485f1cd5da66b7a5d08758805167b1 (sha256 056fbfdf9ee2dc34c7d28dd6b66a73ebcc485f1cd5da66b7a5d08758805167b1), spec_fingerprint 4c792f240f2eddeb1b293e2ff8dcb16085a188074fadafd2384021469481a83a. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 4c792f240f2eddeb1b293e2ff8dcb16085a188074fadafd2384021469481a83a; artifact_sha256: 056fbfdf9ee2dc34c7d28dd6b66a73ebcc485f1cd5da66b7a5d08758805167b1; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/danio_albolineatus_turing_wavelength_s0/danio_albolineatus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=fb3bd6f8d0bd368c..., datasets/danio_albolineatus_turing_wavelength_s0/danio_albolineatus_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=f42000111fe647d8..., datasets/danio_albolineatus_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=80659eeead83362e..., datasets/danio_albolineatus_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=2c0d2a9d801e9099...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing dispersion relation and critical wavenumber. | Short-range melanophore-xanthophore exclusion and long-range dependence (Nakamasu et al. 2009). | Contact-dependent depolarization at xanthophore-melanophore contact (Inaba, Yamanaka & Kondo 2012). | D. albolineatus does not build the reiterated zebrafish stripe stack (Patterson, Bain & Parichy 2014). | Vertical bars versus spots across Danio, with kcnj13 implicated in D. aesculapii (Podobnik et al. 2020).; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters (a, b) = (0.12, 0.88), anisotropy 1.8, activator shrink 1.55, and the two inhibitor ratios. | Identification of the assigned 3.686e-05 m scale with the pearl-danio fastest mode. | Three-seed FFT ensemble and the unstable-band spectral correlation.; transfer_boundary: Sister-species wavelengths are predictions of the diffusion change, not histological measurements at 37 µm. | The aquarium photograph does not resolve 37 µm.; does_not_claim: Sand, plants, and the body outline are not generated by the reaction-diffusion equation. | The unstable-band correlation is not above 0.98. The passing Pearson r is the dispersion identity. | The kinetics are not a cell-by-cell reproduction of Patterson or Volkening.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Addressed. Unstable-band spectral Pearson r is 0.936, lower than the all-band 0.9799. The passing goodness-of-fit remains the dispersion correlation.', 'status': 'addressed'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Addressed. Seeds 3161, 7 and 99 give FFT wavelengths 35759, 34513 and 36860 nm (CV 0.027).', 'status': 'addressed'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Open. Still one photograph. Bounding-box depth/length is not the FishBase landmark.', 'status': 'open'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Open. Still a single assessor.', 'status': 'open'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Open. Sister-species wavelengths are still reconstructions.', 'status': 'open'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.855"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, Pass 2 after R1 and R2)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

